  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-2=-2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-2=-1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-2=0,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-2=1.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14165840/assets/4fc0e4386dd956c2b98c844941ce2e27cd1c9ca8578aca4cf5142e6971911831.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14165840/assets/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png)",
